      "44": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "OUTLETS\n\n• Main\nOutputs a float 2. This can be fed into anything that scales. Most likely a Transform node.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 198.08132934570312,
          "width": 334,
          "x": 286.4986267089844,
          "y": 848.1610717773436
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 0
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
      "45": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "INLETS\n\n• Dimension 1\ninput the desired size, in pixels as a float 2.\n\n• Dimension 2\ninput the size of the texture you want to fit into dimension 1 as a float 2.\n\n• Method\nSets the method used for stretching."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 232.4999084472656,
          "width": 312,
          "x": -67.58341979980469,
          "y": 848.1610717773436
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 0
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
      "46": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "FIT FILL STRETCH\n\nThe Fit Fill Stretch node (FFS) will take two dimensions and fit, fill and or stretch dimension 2 into dimension 1. This is most commonly used with slices from Resolume Arena but can also be used with textures as demonstrated below. \n\nIn the example we render both a circle and a rectangle using the shape render. For the sake of example we resize the rectangle to be 500x500 pixels. The circle is rendered at patch size (1920x1080). Hover over the outlets of the Dimension node to preview the sizes.\nThe FFS node calculates the scaling that needs to happen to fit the circle into the rectangle. These values are given to the Transform node to scale the circle."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 189.4035186767578,
          "width": 1046.9403076171875,
          "x": -67.39404296875,
          "y": 352.2024841308594
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 0
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
